# UW GO environment variables. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
# NEVER put real values in this file: it is the one env file that is committed.
#
# Two categories, and the prefix is what decides which:
#   no prefix    -> server-only. Read at runtime on the server, never sent to the browser.
#                   On Vercel, store as a SECRET / Sensitive value.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ -> inlined into the client bundle at build time and therefore PUBLIC.
#                   On Vercel, store as plain CONFIG. Vercel refuses to mark these
#                   sensitive, because a public prefix cannot be kept private.
#
# So never give a privileged credential a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. The two public values
# below are safe to expose: they are restricted in Google Cloud Console rather than
# kept secret.

# ============================ SERVER-ONLY (Secret) ============================

# Used by /api/routes and /api/geocode only. Never reaches the browser.
# Google Cloud Console -> Credentials -> API key
#   Application restriction: none (or your server IPs if you self-host)
#   API restrictions: Routes API, Geocoding API  (nothing else)
GOOGLE_MAPS_SERVER_KEY=

# ================================ SUPABASE ================================

# Project URL and the anon (publishable) key: Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
# Both are public by design and go in the client bundle; Row Level Security and the
# Waterloo-only database trigger (supabase/migrations) are what protect the data.
# NEVER put the service_role key here or anywhere with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix; this app does not use it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Development only, ignored in production builds: set to 1 to work on the app without a
# Supabase project. Everyone is treated as dev@uwaterloo.ca. Server-side only.
# UWGO_DEV_SKIP_AUTH=1

# ============================== PUBLIC (Config) ==============================

# Renders the map in the browser, so it is necessarily visible in the client bundle.
# It is protected by referrer restrictions, not by secrecy.
#   Application restriction: HTTP referrers, e.g. https://your-domain.example/*,
#     http://localhost:3000/* and http://localhost:3010/*
#   API restrictions: Maps JavaScript API  (nothing else)
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_BROWSER_KEY=

# Optional. A Map ID from Google Cloud Console -> Map Management, rendering type Vector,
# which enables the tilted trip view. A Map ID is a public identifier, not a credential.
# Without it the app falls back to Google's demo map id and stays flat.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=
